vscodium-bin — how to re-pin
  1. Version: the latest release tag at https://github.com/VSCodium/vscodium/releases
     (`gh api repos/VSCodium/vscodium/releases/latest --jq .tag_name`), e.g. 1.135.06055.
     pkgver = that tag, verbatim (it is also the tag in the code.svg source URL).
  2. sha256sums_x86_64 = the first field of the release asset
     https://github.com/VSCodium/vscodium/releases/download/<ver>/VSCodium-linux-x64-<ver>.tar.gz.sha256
     (curl -L; paste by hand).
  3. The code.svg source (last entry of the plain sha256sums) is fetched from the same tag's
     raw URL: `curl -sL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VSCodium/vscodium/refs/tags/<ver>/src/stable/resources/linux/code.svg | sha256sum`.
     The other plain sums (.desktop, .install, .sh, LICENSE) are our vendored files; they change
     only when `dram pkgs update` merges a reviewed AUR diff.
  4. `updpkgsums` downloads the tarball and must print the same sha256 as step 2 (and `gh api
     repos/VSCodium/vscodium/releases/tags/<ver>` shows it as the asset's `digest`) — if it
     differs, the release asset and its .sha256 disagree: stop and look.
